		{"id":"ff1a6ed6efffe761","type":"text","text":"| Option               | Kya karta hai                            | Example                |\n| -------------------- | ---------------------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| `-h`                 | Help menu                                | `hydra -h`             |\n| `-U`                 | Sabhi modules dikhata hai                | `hydra -U`             |\n| `-U <module>`        | Kisi module ki help                      | `hydra -U ssh`         |\n| `-l USER`            | Ek username                              | `hydra -l admin`       |\n| `-L FILE`            | Username list                            | `hydra -L users.txt`   |\n| `-p PASS`            | Ek password                              | `hydra -p Password123` |\n| `-P FILE`            | Password list                            | `hydra -P pass.txt`    |\n| `-C FILE`            | `username:password` file                 | `hydra -C creds.txt`   |\n| `-e nsr`             | Empty, same, reverse password variants   | `hydra -e nsr`         |\n| `-x MIN:MAX:CHARSET` | Pattern se passwords generate            | `hydra -x 6:8:a`       |\n| `-s PORT`            | Custom port                              | `hydra -s 2222`        |\n| `-S`                 | SSL/TLS enable                           | `hydra -S`             |\n| `-4`                 | IPv4 use                                 | `hydra -4`             |\n| `-6`                 | IPv6 use                                 | `hydra -6`             |\n| `-t TASKS`           | Parallel threads                         | `hydra -t 16`          |\n| `-w SEC`             | Connection timeout                       | `hydra -w 10`          |\n| `-W SEC`             | Retry wait                               | `hydra -W 5`           |\n| `-f`                 | First success par stop                   | `hydra -f`             |\n| `-F`                 | Kisi bhi target par success ke baad stop | `hydra -F`             |\n| `-o FILE`            | Output file                              | `hydra -o result.txt`  |\n| `-b FORMAT`          | Output format                            | `hydra -b json`        |\n| `-V`                 | Verbose mode                             | `hydra -V`             |\n| `-vV`                | Very verbose mode                        | `hydra -vV`            |\n| `-d`                 | Debug mode                               | `hydra -d`             |\n| `-q`                 | Quiet mode                               | `hydra -q`             |\n| `-R`                 | Restore session                          | `hydra -R`             |\n| `-I`                 | Ignore restore file                      | `hydra -I`             |\n| `-M FILE`            | Multiple targets                         | `hydra -M hosts.txt`   |\n| `-m OPTS`            | Module-specific                          |                        |\n","x":-578,"y":-518,"width":668,"height":860,"color":"3"},
